{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794344302,"nonce":"f9qaslyJKKKwdJ4ER9NwXyPEFIc=","message":"Measured again with the client's Wayland log only (logging the compositor as well slowed its frame callbacks to about one a second and gave 350 ms medians; those numbers are void). fs-people, Release, key to wl_surface commit, 40 keys per run: idle app 2.7 to 3.6 ms median (max 15 ms); while the keep-alive presents run at 60 Hz (BLINC_KEEP_ALIVE=1) 11 to 12 ms median, max 26 ms, the wait for the frame callback. Tried drawing on the key press itself (handle the frame from the keyboard event, at most one per 4 ms): median 2.9 ms, but 4 of 40 keys per run then took about 1 s, in 4 of 6 runs with keep-alive on, and in none of the runs with it off except one at startup. Present mode mailbox, skipping pre_present_notify and a swapchain latency of 1 or 3 did not remove them. That is the swapchain starvation the code comments describe, so drawing ahead of the frame callback is not safe and was not kept.","files":null}]}